@startuml run-outcome-tracking
!include state-machine-style.iuml
title Slop Machine | Final task and Jira outcome tracking (FR-01)
caption Called after all run executors stop; ticket sync can fail without keeping the execution slot occupied.

state "Persist requested run outcome\nReason, code/PR refs, findings, partial effects\nTask/run/ticket identity and expected status" as Record
state Tracking <<choice>>
state TicketOutcome <<choice>>
state "Verify stage-owned Jira update\nDone, unneeded, dependency blocked or PR pending\nMatch ticket revision, status and evidence links" as VerifyExisting
state "Publish attention or cancellation to Jira\nReason + recovery action; configured status/comment\nCheck ticket revision before mutation" as UpdateTicket
state "Verify prompt-only internal task outcome\nReason, links and current task revision" as VerifyPrompt
state "Reconcile uncertain ticket result\nRead current ticket and operation identity\nBounded retry; avoid duplicate comments/transitions" as Reconcile
state "Outcome synchronized\nTicket or internal status confirmed" as Synced <<success>>
state "Outcome sync pending\nRecord failed update and recovery action\nDo not claim Jira coordination succeeded" as Pending <<attention>>

[*] --> Record
Record --> Tracking : requested outcome persisted
Record --> Pending : durable task outcome cannot be confirmed
Tracking --> TicketOutcome : [Jira ticket linked]
Tracking --> VerifyPrompt : [prompt-only; no Jira ticket]
TicketOutcome --> VerifyExisting : [complete, no_work, dependency_blocked,\nor awaiting_review; stage already updated Jira]
TicketOutcome --> UpdateTicket : [attention or cancelled]
VerifyExisting --> Synced : expected ticket state and links verified
VerifyExisting --> Reconcile : missing, changed or ambiguous ticket state
UpdateTicket --> Synced : Jira outcome update + revision verified
UpdateTicket --> Reconcile : update failed, conflicted or effect unknown
VerifyPrompt --> Synced : internal task status verified
VerifyPrompt --> Pending : update or verification failed
Reconcile --> Synced : expected Jira effect found
Reconcile --> UpdateTicket : [attention/cancelled; safe retry]\nno prior effect; budget remains
Reconcile --> Pending : mismatch or effect unresolved after recovery
Synced --> [*] : return tracking_synced
Pending --> [*] : return tracking_pending

note right of UpdateTicket
  Jira workflow mapping may use a status transition,
  a comment, or both. The record must expose the run's
  resulting state and reason without inventing a Done
  transition or erasing another person's ticket edit.
  All mutations pass through operation-guardrails.puml.
end note
note right of VerifyExisting
  This step verifies stage-owned updates; it does not
  silently repeat a merge, ticket closure or blocked handoff.
  A mismatch prevents the run from claiming a fully
  coordinated successful outcome.
end note
note bottom of Pending
  Executors are already stopped/fenced. Persist the unsynced status,
  operation ID and recovery action, then release the run slot.
  The lifecycle returns attention while Jira sync is pending.
  Recovery must reconcile remote effects before retrying.
end note
@enduml
